                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87422c76-796b-3707-939c-f763df9e97ff",
                        "entry_id": "91ffae45-c8fe-38c4-8469-f69698a0371f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The production of a trill sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea129a84-2fbb-4808-83fa-c3ea3a83d213",
                                "sense_id": "87422c76-796b-3707-939c-f763df9e97ff",
                                "text": "It was pretty close quarters, but I had conversed with her at such length during the nest-building time, that she knew my voice and soon began to answer me in low trillings — trillings that could scarcely be heard — and turn her head to look at me in a friendly way."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7089f905-a974-42a1-9119-c344cba4f9cd",
                                "sense_id": "87422c76-796b-3707-939c-f763df9e97ff",
                                "text": "During the singing act these wing surfaces are moved rapidly on each other, producing the familiar strident trillings of midsummer."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "fdb32199-786d-3a06-a878-3f74cb7ae34b",
                "word": "trilling",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4803ed9f-4992-43b3-9755-5d19e2c274f5",
                        "entry_id": "fdb32199-786d-3a06-a878-3f74cb7ae34b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "trillings"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79caf507-da06-3d48-b995-fd6664e6d647",
                        "entry_id": "fdb32199-786d-3a06-a878-3f74cb7ae34b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A compound crystal consisting of three individuals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2318fa8e-c6f3-443c-b576-8045a181d387",
                                "sense_id": "79caf507-da06-3d48-b995-fd6664e6d647",
                                "text": "Diametrically opposed rays of these stellate groups are of the same optical orientation and the twins are, therefore, trillings ( fig. 29 )."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6f24407-09cf-44e2-8158-35161caa4656",
                                "sense_id": "79caf507-da06-3d48-b995-fd6664e6d647",
                                "text": "Chrysoberyl is orthorhombic in symmetry. Like many orthorhombic minerals, it readily forms an intergrowth with two other individual crystals to make trillings with six sides or, at least, V-shaped twins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d98ae2c2-e890-4498-93fa-64334acbb980",
                                "sense_id": "79caf507-da06-3d48-b995-fd6664e6d647",
                                "text": "In the embryonic stage, pseudohexagonal trillings resemble those of the post-embryonic stage (Figure 2D,E), and are 1 to 3 μm in diameter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a39cd22d-e8a5-3373-a8f6-60ed1100d7f7",
                        "entry_id": "fdb32199-786d-3a06-a878-3f74cb7ae34b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of three offspring born at the same birth; a triplet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "13b422e2-cdbc-4b71-bdf8-3e45b771f62c",
                                "sense_id": "a39cd22d-e8a5-3373-a8f6-60ed1100d7f7",
                                "text": "Every 67th lying-in woman has twins, every 5333rd has trillings, and only every 150,000th has fourlings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60a3ea33-0b7b-4b37-b0b1-7e34722fe72c",
                                "sense_id": "a39cd22d-e8a5-3373-a8f6-60ed1100d7f7",
                                "text": "this breed is prominent for its remarkable fecundity and yield of milk; as a rule, this goat litters once a year and drops 2 kids; occasionally trillings and fourlings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab78a8b0-d054-43cf-825d-ccaacfa977c0",
                                "sense_id": "a39cd22d-e8a5-3373-a8f6-60ed1100d7f7",
                                "text": "About twins and trillings."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
